            <ArticleTitle>[Characteristics of afferent innervation of the ischemic heart and the development of the pain syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain excitation during myocardial ischemia and its electrostimulation were investigated by recording evoked potential and iris movement in cats. It has been demonstrated that pain perception of the heart declines at an early stage of ischemia, but increases noticeably after prolonged and repeated ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
